embeddium.options.added_by_mod_string=Added by mod: %s
embeddium.options.use_quad_normals_for_lighting.name=Use Accurate Quad Shading
embeddium.options.use_quad_normals_for_lighting.tooltip=When enabled, Celeritas will apply shading to non-vanilla block faces based on the true direction they are facing, not their axis-aligned direction. This can improve lighting quality when the Forge experimental light pipeline is disabled (which is recommended for best performance).\n\nIt has no effect if the experimental light pipeline is enabled.
embeddium.options.use_render_pass_optimization.name=Use Render Pass Optimization
embeddium.options.use_render_pass_optimization.tooltip=When enabled, Celeritas will detect block model faces that are marked as transparent (or translucent) when the texture is actually opaque (or transparent) and automatically use a more optimal render pass for them.\n\nThis optimization has no effect when a shader pack is active.
embeddium.options.use_render_pass_consolidation.name=Use Render Pass Consolidation
embeddium.options.use_render_pass_consolidation.tooltip=Combines some vanilla render passes into a single pass. This can very significantly reduce the total number of draw calls needed to render the world, with no visual impact. However, the total amount of rendered geometry will be the same.
embeddium.options.use_faster_clouds.name=Use Faster Clouds
embeddium.options.use_faster_clouds.tooltip=When enabled, Celeritas replaces vanilla cloud rendering with a less glitchy and potentially faster implementation. Disable this if mods' cloud customizations aren't visible.
celeritas.options.async_graph_search.name=Async Occlusion Culling
celeritas.options.async_graph_search.tooltip=Performs occlusion/frustum culling asynchronously, up to one frame behind the current camera position. This can improve frametimes, particularly at higher render distances, but at the cost of chunks popping into view if the camera is turned too aggressively.
celeritas.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.name=Chunk Fade-In Duration
celeritas.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.value=%s ms
celeritas.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.tooltip=Controls how long it takes for newly loaded chunks to fully appear. Longer durations create a smoother transition between unloaded and loaded chunks, reducing visual popping, but may make distant terrain appear to 'fade in' more slowly.
sodium.options.translucent_face_sorting.name=Translucent Face Sorting
sodium.options.translucent_face_sorting.tooltip=If enabled translucent effects from surfaces such as stained glass and water will be applied correctly.
sodium.options.biomeBlendRadius=Biome Blend
